course: dictionary
lesson: 320
title: Angelfish and tropical fish
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An angelfish is a brightly coloured fish with a flat body and long fins. You can find angelfish on coral reefs or in aquariums at home. The word tropical tells you they come from warm parts of the world.
explain: Read the words around the word for clues. «Tropical fish such as angelfish and neon tetras need warm water kept steady by a heater.» The words such as tell you that angelfish is one example of tropical fish.
explain: The word while shows a difference. «While goldfish need cooler water, so they are usually kept apart.» Goldfish and angelfish need different water temperatures, so they are kept in different tanks.
fact: An angelfish is a brightly coloured tropical fish with a flat body and long fins.
fact: Angelfish live on coral reefs or are kept in aquariums.
fact: «Tropical fish such as angelfish» need warm water kept steady by a heater.
fact: A freshwater angelfish lives in fresh water, and a marine angelfish lives in the sea.
fact: The plural of angelfish can be angelfish or angelfishes.
exercise: «Tropical fish such as angelfish and neon tetras need warm water.» What is an angelfish? | A bird that flies over the sea | *A brightly coloured tropical fish with a flat body and long fins | A plant that grows on rocks
exercise: Where might you find an angelfish? | In a bird cage | *On a coral reef or in an aquarium | In a desert
exercise: «While goldfish need cooler water, so they are usually kept apart.» Which fish needs cooler water? | Neon tetras | Angelfish | *Goldfish
test: A marine angelfish lives in which kind of water? | *Salty sea water | Fresh water in a river | Tap water in a bath | Ice
test: Why are goldfish usually kept apart from angelfish? | Goldfish live only in the sea | *They need different water temperatures | Goldfish are always bigger | Angelfish cannot swim
exam: Which word in «Tropical fish such as angelfish and neon tetras» shows that angelfish is one example? | heater | need | steady | *such as
